From fc1c9d43b673e530e33602cfd4747e569c438d1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slopdealer <326519127+slopdealer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:42:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/49] F2: a blob that does not compress is stored in
 compressed form, as stock stores it

Release check F2 (checks/FAILURES.md). Under --compression auto the
tree stored a data blob of 512 KiB or more uncompressed when the
encoder's output was not smaller (the league's ruling 2; repair R4 had
made the rule exact). Such a blob is "uncompressed" in the index. So
`prune --repack-uncompressed` rewrote it on every run and never came
to rest (16,179 blobs before and after a real run on the check's
repository; stock: 0), and `stats` reported compression progress
79.84% where stock's repository reads 100%.

The stored form is stock's again: under every mode but off the
encoder's output is stored, whatever its size. The store-raw rule and
its constant are gone; nothing is decided per blob. The encoder is
still handed a destination of its own worst-case size from 512 KiB on
(compress_presized.go, same bytes as EncodeAll(data, nil)).

Tests: TestCompressionAutoStoresWhatStockStores (was ...NeverStores
MoreThanStock): 80 blobs, 17 of them not shrunk by the encoder, every
one stored in compressed form with stock's size; on the rule it
replaces 15 are stored uncompressed. New
TestPruneRepackUncompressedComesToRest: a repository written without
compression is converted by one prune with RepackUncompressed under
auto, and a second run has nothing to repack; on the rule it replaces
the second run repacks again and the blobs of 512 KiB and more stay
uncompressed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
